   "label": "f01-double-book",
   "front": "Why can two concurrent bookings for the same staff member and time both succeed?",
   "back": "The overlap check is a plain findFirst inside a READ COMMITTED transaction, and the schema has no exclusion constraint. Both transactions can read \"no conflict\" and both insert. Fixes: a Postgres EXCLUDE USING gist constraint on staff and time range, or serializable isolation with retry.",
   "observation": "read-derived",
   "aiTag": false
  },
