   "label": "f02-buffers-and-neighbours",
   "front": "What do service buffers protect against in slot generation, and what do they not protect against?",
   "back": "Buffers are reserved inside the availability window, so a slot keeps its distance from the window edges. The overlap test against existing appointments uses the un-buffered slot, so buffers do not keep a slot away from a neighbouring appointment.",
   "observation": "read-derived",
   "aiTag": false
  },
